PART 5 — THREE THINGS TO KNOW
[SCREEN: Switch to Slide 3]
"Real quick — three things that will save you time."
"One — connect your accounts in settings before you build the routine. Not during. If you try to add Gmail inside the routine builder without connecting it first, it won't be there. Settings first, then build."
"Two — Network Access to Full. I just covered this but it's worth saying again because it's the thing that will make your routine silently fail and you'll have no idea why. Default is Trusted which is too restricted. Change it to Full every time."
"Three — no website logins. If the tool you want to automate doesn't have an API — meaning you normally have to go to a website, log in, and click around to use it — Routines can't do that. It starts completely fresh every run. No saved passwords, no cookies, nothing. Has to be an API."

